will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the reference angle**: The reference angle for \\(-150^\\circ\\) is the positive angle that is coterminal with \\(-150^\\circ\\) and lies between \\(0^\\circ\\) and \\(360^\\circ\\). To find this, we add \\(360^\\circ\\) to \\(-150^\\circ\\):\n   \\[\n   -150^\\circ + 360^\\circ = 210^\\circ\n   \\]\n   So, the reference angle for \\(-150^\\circ\\) is \\(210^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Determine the cosine of the reference angle**: The angle \\(210^\\circ\\) is in the third quadrant. In the third quadrant, the cosine of an angle is negative. The reference angle for \\(210^\\circ\\) is:\n   \\[\n   210^\\circ - 180^\\circ = 30^\\circ\n   \\]\n   Therefore, \\(\\cos(210^\\circ) = -\\cos(30^\\circ)\\). We know that \\(\\cos(30^\\circ) = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\), so:\n   \\[\n   \\cos(210^\\circ) = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(\\cos(-150^\\circ) = \\cos(210^\\circ)\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\cos(-150^\\circ) = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:460"}
